IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ip-nouns`
IMPORT `ip-framework`
IMPORT `ip-rule-of-reason`
IMPORT `ip-restraints`
IMPORT `ip-safety-zone`

-- INDEPENDENT TESTS for the encoding of the Antitrust Guidelines for the Licensing of
-- Intellectual Property (U.S. DOJ and FTC, 12 January 2017). Agency enforcement policy,
-- not law.
--
-- How these were written: the expected answers were written from the source text alone
-- (../../registers/source-bundle/2017-ip-licensing-guidelines.txt, read in full) BEFORE
-- this folder was opened. Only then were the encoding's nouns and rule modules read, in
-- full, bodies and fork comments included, to phrase the facts; the answers were not
-- changed after that. The encoding's own tests were not read. Each group's comment cites
-- the provision and "[pdf page N]" it was read from and the ids of the answers it checks
-- (A1, B6, Example 10 and so on). About ten assertions have no pre-written answer behind
-- them (the direct counts, coverage of mask works and trademarks, n.33, section 6's first
-- sentence, Example 3 with a significant risk or a party-controlled entity, Example 7's
-- empty list of risk factors); every failing assertion has one.
--
-- An assertion that fails here is a FINDING, left failing on purpose: either the
-- encoding departs from the text, or this reader's answer is too strict. The report that
-- accompanies this file says which.
--
-- Added 2026-11-25 by the encoder: one expected value, B6's, was corrected afterwards on
-- the coordinator's instruction, and the comment at it says why. Apart from that and this
-- note, the file is as its author left it (NOTES.md section 11).
--
-- Helpers are prefixed `indep:` so that no name collides with the encoding's.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Helpers
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------

GIVEN t IS A `Type of restraint`
      always IS A BOOLEAN
      integ IS A BOOLEAN
      related IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Restraint in a licensing arrangement`
`indep: restraint` MEANS
    `Restraint in a licensing arrangement` WITH
        `the type of restraint` IS t
        `the restraint is of a kind that would always or almost always tend to reduce output or increase prices` IS always
        `the restraint can be expected to contribute to an efficiency-enhancing integration of economic activity` IS integ
        `the restraint is reasonably related to efficiencies` IS related

-- An ordinary restraint: not a per se type, not of the always-or-almost-always kind,
-- integrative and related to efficiencies.
GIVETH A `Restraint in a licensing arrangement`
`indep: ordinary restraint` MEANS
    `indep: restraint` `a type of restraint not accorded per se treatment` FALSE TRUE TRUE

GIVEN sale IS A BOOLEAN
      excl IS A BOOLEAN
      substance IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Transfer of intellectual property rights (5.7)`
`indep: transfer` MEANS
    `Transfer of intellectual property rights (5.7)` WITH
        `the transfer is an outright sale by the owner of all of its rights to the intellectual property` IS sale
        `the transferee obtains a license that in fact precludes all other persons, including the licensor, from using the licensed intellectual property` IS excl
        `the license in substance transfers intellectual property rights, and its effect may be to substantially lessen competition in a relevant market` IS substance

GIVETH A `Transfer of intellectual property rights (5.7)`
`indep: no transfer` MEANS `indep: transfer` FALSE FALSE FALSE

GIVEN nm IS A STRING
      k IS A `Kind of relevant market`
      licensor IS A NUMBER
      licensees IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A `Relevant market significantly affected by the restraint`
`indep: market with shares` MEANS
    `Relevant market significantly affected by the restraint` WITH
        `the name of the market` IS nm
        `the kind of market` IS k
        `the parties' shares` IS JUST (`Market shares of the licensor and its licensees` WITH `the licensor's share` IS licensor, `the licensees' shares` IS licensees)
        `the other technologies` IS EMPTY
        `the other entities` IS EMPTY

GIVEN nm IS A STRING
      licensor IS A NUMBER
      licensees IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A `Relevant market significantly affected by the restraint`
`indep: goods market` MEANS `indep: market with shares` nm `a goods market` licensor licensees

GIVEN nm IS A STRING
      k IS A `Kind of relevant market`
      techs IS A LIST OF `Other technology`
      ents IS A LIST OF `Other research and development entity`
GIVETH A `Relevant market significantly affected by the restraint`
`indep: market without share data` MEANS
    `Relevant market significantly affected by the restraint` WITH
        `the name of the market` IS nm
        `the kind of market` IS k
        `the parties' shares` IS NOTHING
        `the other technologies` IS techs
        `the other entities` IS ents

GIVEN nm IS A STRING
      controller IS A STRING
      party IS A BOOLEAN
      subst IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Other technology`
`indep: tech` MEANS
    `Other technology` WITH
        `the technology` IS nm
        `who ultimately controls it` IS controller
        `it is controlled by a party to the licensing arrangement` IS party
        `it may be substitutable for the licensed technology at a comparable cost to the user` IS subst

-- A technology controlled by a third party of its own name, substitutable at comparable cost.
GIVEN nm IS A STRING
GIVETH A `Other technology`
`indep: good tech` MEANS `indep: tech` nm nm FALSE TRUE

GIVEN nm IS A STRING
      controller IS A STRING
      party IS A BOOLEAN
      assets IS A BOOLEAN
      incentive IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Other research and development entity`
`indep: entity` MEANS
    `Other research and development entity` WITH
        `the entity` IS nm
        `who ultimately controls it` IS controller
        `it is controlled by a party to the licensing arrangement` IS party
        `it possesses the required specialized assets or characteristics` IS assets
        `it has the incentive to engage in research and development that is a close substitute for that of the parties` IS incentive

GIVEN nm IS A STRING
GIVETH A `Other research and development entity`
`indep: good entity` MEANS `indep: entity` nm nm FALSE TRUE TRUE

GIVEN form IS A `Form of intellectual property`
      inLicensing IS A BOOLEAN
      relatedToUse IS A BOOLEAN
      tr IS A `Transfer of intellectual property rights (5.7)`
      r IS A `Restraint in a licensing arrangement`
      goodsInadequate IS A BOOLEAN
      ms IS A LIST OF `Relevant market significantly affected by the restraint`
GIVETH A `Licensing arrangement before the safety zone (4.3)`
`indep: arrangement in full` MEANS
    `Licensing arrangement before the safety zone (4.3)` WITH
        `the form of the intellectual property licensed` IS form
        `the restraint is in a licensing arrangement` IS inLicensing
        `the restraint is related to the use of the licensed intellectual property` IS relatedToUse
        `the transfer` IS tr
        `the restraint` IS r
        `the analysis of goods markets alone would inadequately address the effects of the arrangement on competition among technologies or in research and development` IS goodsInadequate
        `the relevant markets significantly affected by the restraint` IS ms

-- A patent licence, restraint in the licence and related to the use of the IP, no 5.7
-- transfer.
GIVEN r IS A `Restraint in a licensing arrangement`
      goodsInadequate IS A BOOLEAN
      ms IS A LIST OF `Relevant market significantly affected by the restraint`
GIVETH A `Licensing arrangement before the safety zone (4.3)`
`indep: arrangement` MEANS
    `indep: arrangement in full` `a patent` TRUE TRUE `indep: no transfer` r goodsInadequate ms

GIVEN ms IS A LIST OF `Relevant market significantly affected by the restraint`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Safety zone result (4.3)`
`indep: zone, goods only` MEANS
    `4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`indep: arrangement` `indep: ordinary restraint` FALSE ms)

GIVEN ms IS A LIST OF `Relevant market significantly affected by the restraint`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Safety zone result (4.3)`
`indep: zone, technology or R&D examined` MEANS
    `4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`indep: arrangement` `indep: ordinary restraint` TRUE ms)

GIVETH A `Relevant market significantly affected by the restraint`
`indep: technology market at 50 with four substitutes listed` MEANS
    `Relevant market significantly affected by the restraint` WITH
        `the name of the market` IS "T"
        `the kind of market` IS `a technology market`
        `the parties' shares` IS JUST (`Market shares of the licensor and its licensees` WITH `the licensor's share` IS 50, `the licensees' shares` IS EMPTY)
        `the other technologies` IS (LIST (`indep: good tech` "t1"), (`indep: good tech` "t2"), (`indep: good tech` "t3"), (`indep: good tech` "t4"))
        `the other entities` IS EMPTY

GIVETH A MAYBE `Safety zone result (4.3)`
`indep: INSIDE` MEANS JUST `inside the safety zone: absent extraordinary circumstances, the agencies will not challenge the restraint`

GIVEN res IS A MAYBE `Safety zone result (4.3)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`indep: is outside` MEANS
    CONSIDER res
    WHEN JUST x THEN
        CONSIDER x
        WHEN `outside the safety zone: the agencies will analyze the arrangement on the considerations of parts 3 to 5, and it is not anticompetitive merely for being outside` why THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

GIVEN res IS A MAYBE `Safety zone result (4.3)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`indep: zone does not apply` MEANS
    CONSIDER res
    WHEN JUST x THEN
        CONSIDER x
        WHEN `the safety zone does not apply` why THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- A. Section 4.3, the safety zone [pdf pages 26-27]; n.58, n.59 [pdf page 26];
--    n.60 [pdf page 26]; 5.7, n.85, n.86 [pdf page 36].
-- "Absent extraordinary circumstances, the Agencies will not challenge a restraint ... if
-- (1) the restraint is not facially anticompetitive and (2) the licensor and its licensees
-- collectively account for no more than twenty percent of each relevant market
-- significantly affected by the restraint."
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- A1, A3, A4: "no more than twenty percent": 20 is inside, as are 0 and 19.
#ASSERT (`indep: zone, goods only` (LIST (`indep: goods market` "G" 20 EMPTY))) EQUALS `indep: INSIDE`
#ASSERT (`indep: zone, goods only` (LIST (`indep: goods market` "G" 0 EMPTY))) EQUALS `indep: INSIDE`
#ASSERT (`indep: zone, goods only` (LIST (`indep: goods market` "G" 19 EMPTY))) EQUALS `indep: INSIDE`

-- A2: above twenty is outside.
#ASSERT `indep: is outside` (`indep: zone, goods only` (LIST (`indep: goods market` "G" 20.01 EMPTY)))
#ASSERT `indep: is outside` (`indep: zone, goods only` (LIST (`indep: goods market` "G" 21 EMPTY)))

-- A5, A6: "each relevant market": one market over twenty puts the restraint outside;
-- two at exactly twenty are inside.
#ASSERT `indep: is outside` (`indep: zone, goods only` (LIST (`indep: goods market` "G1" 15 EMPTY), (`indep: goods market` "G2" 25 EMPTY)))
#ASSERT (`indep: zone, goods only` (LIST (`indep: goods market` "G1" 20 EMPTY), (`indep: goods market` "G2" 20 EMPTY))) EQUALS `indep: INSIDE`

-- A8, A9: "collectively account": the licensor's and licensees' shares are summed.
#ASSERT `indep: is outside` (`indep: zone, goods only` (LIST (`indep: goods market` "G" 12 (LIST 9))))
#ASSERT `indep: is outside` (`indep: zone, goods only` (LIST (`indep: goods market` "G" 12 (LIST 5, 4))))
#ASSERT (`indep: zone, goods only` (LIST (`indep: goods market` "G" 12 (LIST 8)))) EQUALS `indep: INSIDE`
#ASSERT (`indep: zone, goods only` (LIST (`indep: goods market` "G" 12 (LIST 4, 4)))) EQUALS `indep: INSIDE`

-- A10, A11: condition (1). n.59: "facially anticompetitive" = restraints that normally
-- warrant per se treatment, and others that would always or almost always reduce output
-- or increase prices. A small share does not save it.
#ASSERT `indep: is outside` (`4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`indep: arrangement` (`indep: restraint` `a type of restraint not accorded per se treatment` TRUE FALSE FALSE) FALSE (LIST (`indep: goods market` "G" 5 EMPTY))))
#ASSERT `indep: is outside` (`4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`indep: arrangement` (`indep: restraint` `naked price-fixing` FALSE FALSE FALSE) FALSE (LIST (`indep: goods market` "G" 5 EMPTY))))
#ASSERT `4.3: the restraint is facially anticompetitive` (`indep: restraint` `naked price-fixing` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `4.3: the restraint is facially anticompetitive` (`indep: restraint` `an output restraint` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `4.3: the restraint is facially anticompetitive` (`indep: restraint` `market division among horizontal competitors` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `4.3: the restraint is facially anticompetitive` (`indep: restraint` `a group boycott of a kind accorded per se treatment` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `4.3: the restraint is facially anticompetitive` (`indep: restraint` `a type of restraint not accorded per se treatment` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`4.3: the restraint is facially anticompetitive` `indep: ordinary restraint`)

-- A12: the zone "does not apply to those transfers of intellectual property rights to
-- which a merger analysis is applied" (4.3, n.60 [pdf page 26]; n.86 [pdf page 36]):
-- an outright sale of all rights, an exclusive licence precluding all others including
-- the licensor (5.7). n.85: a licence that in substance transfers the rights, of which
-- Example 10 is the illustration and in which the Agency "would apply a merger analysis".
#ASSERT `indep: zone does not apply` (`4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`indep: arrangement in full` `a patent` TRUE TRUE (`indep: transfer` TRUE FALSE FALSE) `indep: ordinary restraint` FALSE (LIST (`indep: goods market` "G" 5 EMPTY))))
#ASSERT `indep: zone does not apply` (`4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`indep: arrangement in full` `a patent` TRUE TRUE (`indep: transfer` FALSE TRUE FALSE) `indep: ordinary restraint` FALSE (LIST (`indep: goods market` "G" 5 EMPTY))))
#ASSERT `indep: zone does not apply` (`4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`indep: arrangement in full` `a patent` TRUE TRUE (`indep: transfer` FALSE FALSE TRUE) `indep: ordinary restraint` FALSE (LIST (`indep: goods market` "G" 5 EMPTY))))

-- A13, A14: n.58 [pdf page 26]: the zone does not apply to restraints not in a licensing
-- arrangement, or in one but unrelated to the use of the licensed IP.
#ASSERT `indep: zone does not apply` (`4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`indep: arrangement in full` `a patent` FALSE TRUE `indep: no transfer` `indep: ordinary restraint` FALSE (LIST (`indep: goods market` "G" 5 EMPTY))))
#ASSERT `indep: zone does not apply` (`4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`indep: arrangement in full` `a patent` TRUE FALSE `indep: no transfer` `indep: ordinary restraint` FALSE (LIST (`indep: goods market` "G" 5 EMPTY))))

-- A16: a share outside 0..100 is not a share: NOTHING, never inside or outside.
#ASSERT (`indep: zone, goods only` (LIST (`indep: goods market` "G" 101 EMPTY))) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`indep: zone, goods only` (LIST (`indep: goods market` "G" (-1) EMPTY))) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`indep: zone, goods only` (LIST (`indep: goods market` "G" 5 (LIST 120)))) EQUALS NOTHING

-- A17: share data unavailable for a goods market: 4.3's substitute criteria are for
-- technology and R&D markets only, so the text gives no answer.
#ASSERT (`indep: zone, goods only` (LIST (`indep: market without share data` "G" `a goods market` EMPTY EMPTY))) EQUALS NOTHING

-- A18: no market significantly affected: text silent; vacuously inside or NOTHING are
-- both accepted.
#ASSERT    ((`indep: zone, goods only` EMPTY) EQUALS `indep: INSIDE`) OR ((`indep: zone, goods only` EMPTY) EQUALS NOTHING)

-- A19: "determined by reference only to goods markets unless" goods analysis alone is
-- inadequate [pdf page 26]: a technology market at 50 is not consulted.
#ASSERT (`indep: zone, goods only` (LIST (`indep: goods market` "G" 10 EMPTY), (`indep: market with shares` "T" `a technology market` 50 EMPTY))) EQUALS `indep: INSIDE`
#ASSERT (`indep: zone, goods only` (LIST (`indep: goods market` "G" 10 EMPTY), (`indep: market without share data` "T" `a technology market` (LIST (`indep: good tech` "t1")) EMPTY))) EQUALS `indep: INSIDE`

-- A20: technology examination required and share data available: the twenty-percent
-- test applied to the technology market (NOTHING also accepted).
#ASSERT    (`indep: is outside` (`indep: zone, technology or R&D examined` (LIST (`indep: goods market` "G" 10 EMPTY), (`indep: market with shares` "T" `a technology market` 50 EMPTY)))) OR ((`indep: zone, technology or R&D examined` (LIST (`indep: goods market` "G" 10 EMPTY), (`indep: market with shares` "T" `a technology market` 50 EMPTY))) EQUALS NOTHING)
#ASSERT    ((`indep: zone, technology or R&D examined` (LIST (`indep: goods market` "G" 10 EMPTY), (`indep: market with shares` "T" `a technology market` 15 EMPTY))) EQUALS `indep: INSIDE`) OR ((`indep: zone, technology or R&D examined` (LIST (`indep: goods market` "G" 10 EMPTY), (`indep: market with shares` "T" `a technology market` 15 EMPTY))) EQUALS NOTHING)

-- A21 to A26: 4.3 [pdf pages 26-27], technology market without reliable share data:
-- "four or more independently controlled technologies in addition to the technologies
-- controlled by the parties ... that may be substitutable for the licensed technology at
-- a comparable cost to the user".
#ASSERT (`indep: zone, technology or R&D examined` (LIST (`indep: goods market` "G" 10 EMPTY), (`indep: market without share data` "T" `a technology market` (LIST (`indep: good tech` "t1"), (`indep: good tech` "t2"), (`indep: good tech` "t3"), (`indep: good tech` "t4")) EMPTY))) EQUALS `indep: INSIDE`
#ASSERT `indep: is outside` (`indep: zone, technology or R&D examined` (LIST (`indep: market without share data` "T" `a technology market` (LIST (`indep: good tech` "t1"), (`indep: good tech` "t2"), (`indep: good tech` "t3")) EMPTY)))
-- A23: five technologies, two controlled by the parties: three count.
#ASSERT `indep: is outside` (`indep: zone, technology or R&D examined` (LIST (`indep: market without share data` "T" `a technology market` (LIST (`indep: good tech` "t1"), (`indep: good tech` "t2"), (`indep: good tech` "t3"), (`indep: tech` "t4" "Licensor" TRUE TRUE), (`indep: tech` "t5" "Licensee" TRUE TRUE)) EMPTY)))
-- A24: four technologies, two under one controller: not four independently controlled.
#ASSERT `indep: is outside` (`indep: zone, technology or R&D examined` (LIST (`indep: market without share data` "T" `a technology market` (LIST (`indep: good tech` "t1"), (`indep: good tech` "t2"), (`indep: tech` "t3" "X Corp" FALSE TRUE), (`indep: tech` "t4" "X Corp" FALSE TRUE)) EMPTY)))
-- A25: one of four not substitutable at a comparable cost.
#ASSERT `indep: is outside` (`indep: zone, technology or R&D examined` (LIST (`indep: market without share data` "T" `a technology market` (LIST (`indep: good tech` "t1"), (`indep: good tech` "t2"), (`indep: good tech` "t3"), (`indep: tech` "t4" "t4" FALSE FALSE)) EMPTY)))
-- A26: four qualifying, but the restraint is facially anticompetitive.
#ASSERT `indep: is outside` (`4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`indep: arrangement` (`indep: restraint` `a type of restraint not accorded per se treatment` TRUE FALSE FALSE) TRUE (LIST (`indep: market without share data` "T" `a technology market` (LIST (`indep: good tech` "t1"), (`indep: good tech` "t2"), (`indep: good tech` "t3"), (`indep: good tech` "t4")) EMPTY))))
-- The count itself.
#ASSERT (`the number of independently controlled technologies in addition to those of the parties that may be substitutable at a comparable cost` (LIST (`indep: good tech` "t1"), (`indep: good tech` "t2"), (`indep: tech` "t3" "Licensor" TRUE TRUE), (`indep: tech` "t4" "t4" FALSE FALSE))) EQUALS 2

-- A27 to A30: R&D market without reliable share data [pdf page 27]: "four or more
-- independently controlled entities in addition to the parties ... possess the required
-- specialized assets or characteristics and the incentive".
#ASSERT (`indep: zone, technology or R&D examined` (LIST (`indep: market without share data` "R" `a research and development market` EMPTY (LIST (`indep: good entity` "e1"), (`indep: good entity` "e2"), (`indep: good entity` "e3"), (`indep: good entity` "e4"))))) EQUALS `indep: INSIDE`
#ASSERT `indep: is outside` (`indep: zone, technology or R&D examined` (LIST (`indep: market without share data` "R" `a research and development market` EMPTY (LIST (`indep: good entity` "e1"), (`indep: good entity` "e2"), (`indep: good entity` "e3")))))
#ASSERT `indep: is outside` (`indep: zone, technology or R&D examined` (LIST (`indep: market without share data` "R" `a research and development market` EMPTY (LIST (`indep: good entity` "e1"), (`indep: good entity` "e2"), (`indep: good entity` "e3"), (`indep: entity` "e4" "e4" FALSE TRUE FALSE)))))
#ASSERT `indep: is outside` (`indep: zone, technology or R&D examined` (LIST (`indep: market without share data` "R" `a research and development market` EMPTY (LIST (`indep: good entity` "e1"), (`indep: good entity` "e2"), (`indep: good entity` "e3"), (`indep: entity` "e4" "e4" FALSE FALSE TRUE)))))

-- A31: share data available and accurate in a technology market: the count criterion
-- does not apply, so four substitutes do not bring a 50 percent share inside.
#ASSERT NOT ((`indep: zone, technology or R&D examined` (LIST `indep: technology market at 50 with four substitutes listed`)) EQUALS `indep: INSIDE`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- More helpers, for parts 3 to 6
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------

GIVEN noEffect IS A BOOLEAN
      alternative IS A BOOLEAN
      necessary IS A BOOLEAN
      tooLong IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Findings under the rule of reason`
`indep: findings` MEANS
    `Findings under the rule of reason` WITH
        `the agencies conclude that the restraint is unlikely to have an anticompetitive effect` IS noEffect
        `it is clear that the parties could have achieved similar efficiencies by practical and significantly less restrictive means` IS alternative
        `the restraint is reasonably necessary to achieve procompetitive efficiencies` IS necessary
        `the duration of the restraint clearly exceeds the period needed to achieve the procompetitive efficiency` IS tooLong

GIVEN actual IS A BOOLEAN
      potential IS A BOOLEAN
      complementary IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Two parties in a relevant market (3.3)`
`indep: two parties` MEANS
    `Two parties in a relevant market (3.3)` WITH
        `the market` IS "M"
        `they would have been actual competitors in the market in the absence of the license` IS actual
        `it is reasonably probable that one would have become a competitor of the other in the market in the absence of the licensing arrangement` IS potential
        `the arrangement affects activities of theirs in the market that are in a complementary relationship` IS complementary

GIVEN subst IS A BOOLEAN
      blocked IS A BOOLEAN
      licensesOthers IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Two parties' technologies (3.2.2)`
`indep: two technologies` MEANS
    `Two parties' technologies (3.2.2)` WITH
        `the other party controls a technology or good close enough a substitute to constrain significantly the exercise of market power with respect to the licensed technology` IS subst
        `one party's technology cannot be practiced without using the other's` IS blocked
        `either party licenses its technology to others` IS licensesOthers

GIVEN exclTerms IS A BOOLEAN
      exclStructure IS A BOOLEAN
      dealingTerm IS A BOOLEAN
      dealingCost IS A BOOLEAN
      otherRestraint IS A BOOLEAN
      single IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `License terms and structure (4.1.2)`
`indep: licence` MEANS
    `License terms and structure (4.1.2)` WITH
        `the license by its terms is exclusive or partially exclusive, limiting the licensor's ability to license others` IS exclTerms
        `the license is structured so that the licensor is unlikely to license others or to practice the technology itself` IS exclStructure
        `a term of the license prevents or restrains the licensee from licensing, selling, distributing or using competing technologies` IS dealingTerm
        `the license is structured to increase significantly the licensee's cost when it uses competing technologies` IS dealingCost
        `the license contains another restraint on the competitive conduct of the licensor or the licensee` IS otherRestraint
        `a party chooses to deal with a single licensor or licensee` IS single
        `a party confines its activity to a single field of use or location` IS single
        `only a single licensee has chosen to take a license` IS single
        `some or all of the potential licensees choose to use the licensed technology to the exclusion of other technologies` IS single

GIVEN amongLicensors IS A BOOLEAN
      amongLicensees IS A BOOLEAN
      licensorLicensee IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Horizontal relationships among the parties (4.1.2)`
`indep: horizontals` MEANS
    `Horizontal relationships among the parties (4.1.2)` WITH
        `there is a horizontal relationship among licensors` IS amongLicensors
        `there is a horizontal relationship among licensees` IS amongLicensees
        `there is a horizontal relationship between the licensor and a licensee` IS licensorLicensee

GIVEN marketed IS A BOOLEAN
      dataAvailable IS A BOOLEAN
      comparable IS A BOOLEAN
      n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Technology-market facts (3.2.2)`
`indep: technology facts` MEANS
    `Technology-market facts (3.2.2)` WITH
        `the rights to the intellectual property are marketed separately from the products in which they are used` IS marketed
        `market share data or other indicia of market power are available` IS dataAvailable
        `the competing technologies appear comparably efficient` IS comparable
        `the number of technologies in the market, the licensed technology included` IS n

GIVEN adverse IS A BOOLEAN
      associated IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Research and development facts (3.2.3)`
`indep: R&D facts` MEANS
    `Research and development facts (3.2.3)` WITH
        `the arrangement may adversely affect competition to develop new or improved goods or processes` IS adverse
        `the capabilities to engage in the relevant research and development can be associated with specialized assets or characteristics of specific firms` IS associated
        `the entities have comparable capabilities and incentives to pursue research and development that is a close substitute for that of the parties` IS TRUE
        `the number of entities in the research and development market, the parties included` IS 5

GIVEN conditioned IS A BOOLEAN
      power IS A BOOLEAN
      protected IS A BOOLEAN
      adverse IS A BOOLEAN
      outweigh IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Tying facts (5.3)`
`indep: tying` MEANS
    `Tying facts (5.3)` WITH
        `the license of one item is conditioned on the licensee's purchase or license of another, separate item` IS conditioned
        `the seller has market power in the tying product` IS power
        `the tying item is protected by a patent, copyright or trade secret` IS protected
        `the arrangement has an adverse effect on competition in the relevant market for the tying product or the tied product` IS adverse
        `efficiency justifications for the arrangement outweigh its anticompetitive effects` IS outweigh

GIVEN isGrantback IS A BOOLEAN
      exclusive IS A BOOLEAN
      power IS A BOOLEAN
      reduces IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Grantback facts (5.6)`
`indep: grantback` MEANS
    `Grantback facts (5.6)` WITH
        `the licensee agrees to extend to the licensor the right to use the licensee's improvements to the licensed technology` IS isGrantback
        `the grantback is exclusive` IS exclusive
        `the licensor has market power in a relevant technology or research and development market` IS power
        `the grantback provision is likely to reduce significantly licensees' incentives to invest in improving the licensed technology` IS reduces
        `it promotes dissemination of licensees' improvements to the licensed technology` IS FALSE
        `it increases the licensors' incentives to disseminate the licensed technology` IS FALSE
        `it otherwise increases competition and output in a relevant technology or research and development market` IS FALSE
        `grantback provisions in the relevant markets generally increase licensors' incentives to innovate in the first place` IS FALSE

GIVEN enforcement IS A BOOLEAN
      invalid IS A BOOLEAN
      fraud IS A BOOLEAN
      inequitable IS A BOOLEAN
      elements IS A BOOLEAN
      sham IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Enforcement of intellectual property rights (6)`
`indep: enforcement` MEANS
    `Enforcement of intellectual property rights (6)` WITH
        `the conduct is actual or attempted enforcement of the rights` IS enforcement
        `the rights enforced are invalid` IS invalid
        `the patent was obtained by knowing and willful fraud on the Patent and Trademark Office` IS fraud
        `the patent was obtained by inequitable conduct before the Patent and Trademark Office` IS inequitable
        `all the other elements necessary to establish the charge are proved` IS elements
        `the enforcement is by sham litigation` IS sham

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- B. Section 3.4, per se or rule of reason [pdf pages 19-20]; 5.1 [pdf page 28].
-- "If there is no efficiency-enhancing integration of economic activity and if the type
-- of restraint is one that has been accorded per se treatment, the Agencies will
-- challenge the restraint under the per se rule. Otherwise, the Agencies will apply a
-- rule of reason analysis."
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- B1: each per se type, no integration: the per se rule.
#ASSERT (`3.4: the mode of analysis` (`indep: restraint` `naked price-fixing` FALSE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS `the agencies will challenge the restraint under the per se rule`
#ASSERT (`3.4: the mode of analysis` (`indep: restraint` `an output restraint` FALSE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS `the agencies will challenge the restraint under the per se rule`
#ASSERT (`3.4: the mode of analysis` (`indep: restraint` `market division among horizontal competitors` FALSE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS `the agencies will challenge the restraint under the per se rule`
#ASSERT (`3.4: the mode of analysis` (`indep: restraint` `a group boycott of a kind accorded per se treatment` FALSE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS `the agencies will challenge the restraint under the per se rule`
-- B2: a per se type WITH integration: rule of reason.
#ASSERT (`3.4: the mode of analysis` (`indep: restraint` `naked price-fixing` FALSE TRUE FALSE)) EQUALS `the agencies will apply a rule of reason analysis`
-- B3: not a per se type, no integration: rule of reason.
#ASSERT (`3.4: the mode of analysis` (`indep: restraint` `a type of restraint not accorded per se treatment` FALSE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS `the agencies will apply a rule of reason analysis`
-- B1 again through the outcome function.
#ASSERT (`3.4: what the agencies do with the restraint` (`indep: restraint` `market division among horizontal competitors` FALSE FALSE FALSE) (`indep: findings` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS (JUST `the agencies will challenge the restraint under the per se rule, without an elaborate inquiry into its likely competitive effect`)
-- B4: [pdf page 20] "If the Agencies conclude that a restraint has no likely anticompetitive
-- effects, they will treat it as reasonable".
#ASSERT (`3.4: what the agencies do with the restraint` `indep: ordinary restraint` (`indep: findings` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS (JUST `the agencies will treat the restraint as reasonable, without an elaborate analysis of market power or the justifications for it`)
-- B5: [pdf page 20] facially of a kind always or almost always to reduce output or
-- increase prices, and not reasonably related to efficiencies: likely challenge without
-- elaborate analysis.
#ASSERT (`3.4: what the agencies do with the restraint` (`indep: restraint` `a type of restraint not accorded per se treatment` TRUE TRUE FALSE) (`indep: findings` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS (JUST `the agencies will likely challenge the restraint without an elaborate analysis of particular industry circumstances`)
-- B6: the same kind but reasonably related to efficiencies: this reader wrote "text
-- silent on outcome: NOTHING".
-- CORRECTED 2026-11-25 by the encoder of legalese-2026-11, on the coordinator's
-- instruction; the only expected value in this file changed after it was written. The
-- reader's NOTHING was wrong: with integration and no per se type, 3.4 [pdf page 19] says
-- "Otherwise, the Agencies will apply a rule of reason analysis", and "Application of the
-- rule of reason requires an inquiry into the likely competitive effects" (n.48: "See
-- sections 4.1-4.3"). The quick look of [pdf page 20] needs a restraint "not reasonably
-- related to efficiencies", which this one is, so it does not speak; the text's outcome
-- is the inquiry, not silence.
#ASSERT (`3.4: what the agencies do with the restraint` (`indep: restraint` `a type of restraint not accorded per se treatment` TRUE TRUE TRUE) (`indep: findings` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS (JUST `the agencies inquire into the likely competitive effects, in an inquiry meet for the case, as in part 4`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- C. Section 4.2, efficiencies and justifications [pdf pages 25-26].
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- C1: "If the Agencies conclude ... that a restraint ... is unlikely to have an
-- anticompetitive effect, they will not challenge the restraint", whatever else is found.
#ASSERT (`4.2: what the agencies do on their findings` (`indep: findings` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS (JUST `the agencies will not challenge the restraint`)
#ASSERT (`4.2: what the agencies do on their findings` (`indep: findings` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)) EQUALS (JUST `the agencies will not challenge the restraint`)
-- C2: likely anticompetitive, not reasonably necessary, no clear alternative: accept
-- NOTHING (the encoding's result type has no "challenge" value).
#ASSERT (`4.2: what the agencies do on their findings` (`indep: findings` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- C3: reasonably necessary: balance.
#ASSERT (`4.2: what the agencies do on their findings` (`indep: findings` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)) EQUALS (JUST `the agencies will balance the procompetitive efficiencies and the anticompetitive effects to determine the probable net effect on competition in each relevant market`)
-- C4: "If it is clear that the parties could have achieved similar efficiencies by means
-- that are significantly less restrictive, then the Agencies will not give weight to the
-- parties' efficiency claim." Unconditioned: asserted with necessity FALSE and TRUE.
#ASSERT (`4.2: what the agencies do on their findings` (`indep: findings` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS (JUST `the agencies will not give weight to the parties' efficiency claim`)
#ASSERT (`4.2: what the agencies do on their findings` (`indep: findings` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)) EQUALS (JUST `the agencies will not give weight to the parties' efficiency claim`)
-- C5: duration that clearly exceeds the period needed bears on reasonable necessity.
#ASSERT elem `a duration clearly exceeding the period needed to achieve the efficiency` (`4.2: the considerations against reasonable necessity that are present` (`indep: findings` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (elem `a duration clearly exceeding the period needed to achieve the efficiency` (`4.2: the considerations against reasonable necessity that are present` (`indep: findings` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)))

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- D. Relationships, markets and exclusivity: 3.3 [pdf pages 16-17], n.27 [pdf page 10],
--    3.2.2 [pdf pages 11-12], n.37 [pdf page 12], 3.2.3 [pdf page 14],
--    4.1.1 [pdf page 22], 4.1.2 [pdf pages 22-24].
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- D1: actual competitors absent the licence, and complementary: horizontal component
-- "even if a vertical relationship also exists".
#ASSERT `3.3: the relationship has a horizontal component` (`indep: two parties` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT (`3.3: the relationship of the parties in the market` (`indep: two parties` TRUE FALSE TRUE)) EQUALS `a relationship horizontal in part and vertical in part`
-- D2: n.27: a potential competitor (reasonably probable) is enough.
#ASSERT `3.3: the relationship has a horizontal component` (`indep: two parties` FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`3.3: the relationship has a horizontal component` (`indep: two parties` FALSE FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT (`3.3: the relationship of the parties in the market` (`indep: two parties` FALSE FALSE TRUE)) EQUALS `a vertical relationship`

-- D4: [pdf page 23] exclusive licences "may raise antitrust concerns only if there is a
-- horizontal relationship"; none here.
#ASSERT (`4.1.2: what the agencies say of the license's exclusivity` (`indep: licence` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) (`indep: horizontals` FALSE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS (JUST `generally, the exclusive licensing raises no antitrust concern: there is no horizontal relationship among licensors, among licensees, or between the licensor and a licensee`)
-- D5: [pdf page 23] a non-exclusive licence with no restraint on competitive conduct:
-- generally no concern "even if the parties to the license are in a horizontal
-- relationship".
#ASSERT (`4.1.2: what the agencies say of the license's exclusivity` (`indep: licence` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) (`indep: horizontals` TRUE TRUE TRUE)) EQUALS (JUST `generally, the non-exclusive license does not present antitrust concerns: it contains no restraint on the competitive conduct of the licensor or the licensee`)
-- D6: [pdf page 24] de facto exclusivity of both kinds.
#ASSERT `4.1.2: the license has the effect of exclusive licensing` (`indep: licence` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `4.1.2: the license has the effect of exclusive dealing` (`indep: licence` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- D7, D8: [pdf pages 22, 24] a single licensee, a single field, or licensees' own choice
-- to use only the licensed technology do not by themselves make exclusivity.
#ASSERT NOT (`4.1.2: the license has the effect of exclusive licensing` (`indep: licence` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`4.1.2: the license has the effect of exclusive dealing` (`indep: licence` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT (`4.1.2: what the agencies say of the license's exclusivity` (`indep: licence` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE) (`indep: horizontals` TRUE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS (JUST `generally, the non-exclusive license does not present antitrust concerns: it contains no restraint on the competitive conduct of the licensor or the licensee`)

-- D10: [pdf page 12] no share data or other indicia, comparably efficient technologies:
-- "the Agencies will assign each technology the same market share".
#ASSERT (`3.2.2: the market share the agencies will assign to each technology` (`indep: technology facts` TRUE FALSE TRUE 4)) EQUALS (JUST 25)
#ASSERT (`3.2.2: the market share the agencies will assign to each technology` (`indep: technology facts` TRUE FALSE TRUE 5)) EQUALS (JUST 20)
-- D10, its conditions: data available, or not comparably efficient: no rule stated.
#ASSERT (`3.2.2: the market share the agencies will assign to each technology` (`indep: technology facts` TRUE TRUE TRUE 4)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`3.2.2: the market share the agencies will assign to each technology` (`indep: technology facts` TRUE FALSE FALSE 4)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- D11: [pdf page 14] "only when the capabilities ... can be associated with specialized
-- assets or characteristics of specific firms".
#ASSERT (`3.2.3: whether a research and development market is analysed` (`indep: R&D facts` TRUE FALSE)) EQUALS (JUST `the agencies will not delineate a research and development market`)
#ASSERT (`3.2.3: whether a research and development market is analysed` (`indep: R&D facts` TRUE TRUE)) EQUALS (JUST `the agencies may analyse the impact as a competitive effect in a separate research and development market`)
-- 3.2.2 [pdf page 11]; n.33: IP licensed as an integral part of a marketed good needs no
-- separate technology-market analysis.
#ASSERT (`3.2.2: whether a technology market is analysed` (`indep: technology facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE 1)) EQUALS `there is no need for a separate analysis of technology markets`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- E. Part 5 [pdf pages 28-37].
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- E1: 5.2 [pdf pages 29-30] price maintenance: rule of reason; a horizontal cartel is per
-- se illegal.
#ASSERT (`5.2: price maintenance` (`Price maintenance facts (5.2)` WITH `the licensor conditions the license on the resale price of the product incorporating the licensed technology` IS TRUE, `the agreement constitutes a horizontal cartel` IS FALSE)) EQUALS (JUST `the agencies will apply a rule of reason analysis, case by case, evaluating the competitive benefits and harms`)
#ASSERT (`5.2: price maintenance` (`Price maintenance facts (5.2)` WITH `the licensor conditions the license on the resale price of the product incorporating the licensed technology` IS TRUE, `the agreement constitutes a horizontal cartel` IS TRUE)) EQUALS (JUST `the agencies will consider the agreement per se illegal: it constitutes a horizontal cartel`)

-- E2: 5.3 [pdf pages 30-31]: all three conditions: likely challenge.
#ASSERT (`5.3: tying` (`indep: tying` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)) EQUALS (JUST `the agencies would be likely to challenge the tying arrangement`)
-- E2 / D12: no presumption of market power from a patent, copyright or trade secret
-- (2.2 [pdf page 6]; 5.3 [pdf page 31]): protected, but no market power found.
#ASSERT NOT ((`5.3: tying` (`indep: tying` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)) EQUALS (JUST `the agencies would be likely to challenge the tying arrangement`))
-- E2: efficiencies outweigh: not the likely-challenge outcome.
#ASSERT NOT ((`5.3: tying` (`indep: tying` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)) EQUALS (JUST `the agencies would be likely to challenge the tying arrangement`))
-- E3: a package licence is a tie only if one licence is conditioned on another.
#ASSERT `5.3: the arrangement is a tying arrangement` (`indep: tying` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`5.3: the arrangement is a tying arrangement` (`indep: tying` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE))

-- E4: 5.4 [pdf page 31] exclusive dealing: rule of reason.
#ASSERT (`5.4: exclusive dealing` (`indep: licence` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS (JUST `exclusive dealing arrangements are evaluated under the rule of reason`)

-- E5: 5.5 [pdf page 32] pools as mechanisms for naked price-fixing or market division:
-- per se.
#ASSERT (`5.5: the mode of analysis of a collective restraint in a pool or cross-license` (`indep: restraint` `naked price-fixing` FALSE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS `the agencies will challenge the restraint under the per se rule`
#ASSERT (`5.5: the mode of analysis of a collective restraint in a pool or cross-license` (`indep: restraint` `market division among horizontal competitors` FALSE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS `the agencies will challenge the restraint under the per se rule`

-- E6: 5.5 [pdf page 33] exclusion from a pool among competing technologies: unlikely
-- anticompetitive UNLESS both conditions; with both, evaluate.
#ASSERT (`5.5: exclusion from a pool or cross-license` (`Exclusion from a pool or cross-license (5.5)` WITH `the arrangement is among competing technologies` IS TRUE, `excluded firms cannot effectively compete in the relevant market for the good incorporating the licensed technologies` IS TRUE, `the pool participants collectively possess market power in the relevant market` IS TRUE)) EQUALS (JUST `the agencies will evaluate whether the limitations on participation are reasonably related to the efficient development and exploitation of the pooled technologies, and will assess their net effect in the relevant market`)
#ASSERT (`5.5: exclusion from a pool or cross-license` (`Exclusion from a pool or cross-license (5.5)` WITH `the arrangement is among competing technologies` IS TRUE, `excluded firms cannot effectively compete in the relevant market for the good incorporating the licensed technologies` IS TRUE, `the pool participants collectively possess market power in the relevant market` IS FALSE)) EQUALS (JUST `exclusion is unlikely to have anticompetitive effects`)
#ASSERT (`5.5: exclusion from a pool or cross-license` (`Exclusion from a pool or cross-license (5.5)` WITH `the arrangement is among competing technologies` IS TRUE, `excluded firms cannot effectively compete in the relevant market for the good incorporating the licensed technologies` IS FALSE, `the pool participants collectively possess market power in the relevant market` IS TRUE)) EQUALS (JUST `exclusion is unlikely to have anticompetitive effects`)

-- E7: 5.5 [pdf page 33] grant of current and future technology at minimal cost: a problem
-- only when a large fraction of potential R&D is included.
#ASSERT (`5.5: a pool's grant of current and future technology at minimal cost` (`Pool terms on future technology (5.5)` WITH `the pooling arrangement requires members to grant licenses to each other for current and future technology at minimal cost` IS TRUE, `the arrangement includes a large fraction of the potential research and development in a research and development market` IS FALSE)) EQUALS (JUST `the arrangement is not likely to cause competitive problems: it does not include a large fraction of the potential research and development in a research and development market`)
#ASSERT NOT ((`5.5: a pool's grant of current and future technology at minimal cost` (`Pool terms on future technology (5.5)` WITH `the pooling arrangement requires members to grant licenses to each other for current and future technology at minimal cost` IS TRUE, `the arrangement includes a large fraction of the potential research and development in a research and development market` IS TRUE)) EQUALS (JUST `the arrangement is not likely to cause competitive problems: it does not include a large fraction of the potential research and development in a research and development market`))

-- E8: 5.5 [pdf page 32] settlement cross-licence among horizontal competitors: "In the
-- absence of offsetting efficiencies, such settlements may be challenged".
#ASSERT (`5.5: a settlement by cross-license` (`Settlement by cross-license (5.5)` WITH `the settlement involves the cross-licensing of intellectual property rights between horizontal competitors` IS TRUE, `the effect of the settlement is to diminish competition among entities that would have been actual or potential competitors in a relevant market in the absence of the cross-license` IS TRUE, `there are offsetting efficiencies` IS FALSE)) EQUALS (JUST `the agencies may challenge the settlement as an unlawful restraint of trade`)
#ASSERT NOT ((`5.5: a settlement by cross-license` (`Settlement by cross-license (5.5)` WITH `the settlement involves the cross-licensing of intellectual property rights between horizontal competitors` IS TRUE, `the effect of the settlement is to diminish competition among entities that would have been actual or potential competitors in a relevant market in the absence of the cross-license` IS TRUE, `there are offsetting efficiencies` IS TRUE)) EQUALS (JUST `the agencies may challenge the settlement as an unlawful restraint of trade`))

-- E9: 5.6 [pdf pages 35-36] grantbacks: rule of reason; exclusivity and the licensor's
-- market power are matters weighed.
#ASSERT (`5.6: a grantback` (`indep: grantback` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS (JUST `the agencies will evaluate the grantback provision under the rule of reason`)
#ASSERT elem `the exclusivity of the grantback` (`5.6: the matters present` (`indep: grantback` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT elem `the licensor's market power in a relevant technology or research and development market` (`5.6: the matters present` (`indep: grantback` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE))

-- E10, E11: 5.7 [pdf page 36] merger analysis.
#ASSERT (`5.7: merger analysis of the transfer` (`indep: transfer` TRUE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS `the agencies will apply a merger analysis: an outright sale of all rights to the intellectual property`
#ASSERT (`5.7: merger analysis of the transfer` (`indep: transfer` FALSE TRUE FALSE)) EQUALS `the agencies will apply a merger analysis: an exclusive license`
#ASSERT (`5.7: merger analysis of the transfer` `indep: no transfer`) EQUALS `section 5.7 calls for no merger analysis`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- F. Part 6, invalid or unenforceable rights [pdf pages 37-38]. Membership only: the
--    text gives no order.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- F1: fraud on the PTO with all other elements: may violate Sherman 2 or FTC Act 5.
#ASSERT elem `it may violate section 2 of the Sherman Act or section 5 of the Federal Trade Commission Act` (`6: what section 6 says of the enforcement` (`indep: enforcement` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE))
-- F1: fraud, but the other elements not proved: not that statement.
#ASSERT NOT (elem `it may violate section 2 of the Sherman Act or section 5 of the Federal Trade Commission Act` (`6: what section 6 says of the enforcement` (`indep: enforcement` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)))
-- F2: inequitable conduct without knowing and willful fraud: not a basis of a section 2
-- claim.
#ASSERT elem `the inequitable conduct will not be the basis of a section 2 claim` (`6: what section 6 says of the enforcement` (`indep: enforcement` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE))
-- F3: inequitable conduct that is also knowing and willful fraud, other elements present.
#ASSERT NOT (elem `the inequitable conduct will not be the basis of a section 2 claim` (`6: what section 6 says of the enforcement` (`indep: enforcement` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)))
-- F4: inequitable conduct short of fraud may violate section 5 under some circumstances.
#ASSERT elem `under some circumstances it may violate section 5 of the Federal Trade Commission Act` (`6: what section 6 says of the enforcement` (`indep: enforcement` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE))
-- F5: sham litigation.
#ASSERT elem `sham litigation may constitute an element of a violation of the Sherman Act` (`6: what section 6 says of the enforcement` (`indep: enforcement` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE))
-- 6, first sentence: enforcement of invalid rights may be challenged.
#ASSERT elem `the agencies may challenge the enforcement of invalid intellectual property rights as an antitrust violation` (`6: what section 6 says of the enforcement` (`indep: enforcement` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- G. The ten numbered Examples. The facts are set from the Example's Situation and
--    Discussion; where a fact is the agencies' finding in the Discussion, it is set as
--    the Discussion finds it, and the comment says so.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Example 1 [pdf pages 8-9]: ComputerCo's field-of-use and territorial licences, no term
-- deterring licensees from other programs, licensees not competitors: "The Agency
-- therefore would be unlikely to object". Field-of-use and territorial licences are the
-- "partially exclusive licenses" of 4.1.2; no horizontal relationship.
#ASSERT (`4.1.2: what the agencies say of the license's exclusivity` (`indep: licence` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) (`indep: horizontals` FALSE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS (JUST `generally, the exclusive licensing raises no antitrust concern: there is no horizontal relationship among licensors, among licensees, or between the licensor and a licensee`)
-- Example 1, n.22: the same whether the program is protected by patent, copyright or
-- trade secret.
#ASSERT (`1.0: whether the guidelines cover licensing of` `a patent`) EQUALS `covered by these guidelines`
#ASSERT (`1.0: whether the guidelines cover licensing of` `a copyright`) EQUALS `covered by these guidelines`
#ASSERT (`1.0: whether the guidelines cover licensing of` `a trade secret`) EQUALS `covered by these guidelines`
#ASSERT (`1.0: whether the guidelines cover licensing of` `a mask work fixed in a semiconductor chip product`) EQUALS `covered by these guidelines`
#ASSERT (`1.0: whether the guidelines cover licensing of` `a trademark`) EQUALS `not covered: these guidelines do not cover the antitrust treatment of trademarks`
-- Example 1 variant: the licence bars use of any other inventory program: exclusive
-- dealing, so the conclusion "could differ": rule of reason (5.4).
#ASSERT (`5.4: exclusive dealing` (`indep: licence` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS (JUST `exclusive dealing arrangements are evaluated under the rule of reason`)

-- Example 2 [pdf pages 11-13]: Alpha and Beta's process technologies, licensable to
-- third parties apart from the drug: the Agency "would delineate a technology market".
-- (Reader's mapping: the processes could be licensed to third parties, so the rights are
-- marketed apart from the drug.) The outcome of that analysis is not given.
#ASSERT (`3.2.2: whether a technology market is analysed` (`indep: technology facts` TRUE FALSE FALSE 3)) EQUALS `the agencies may analyse the competitive effects of the arrangement in a technology market`

-- Example 3 [pdf pages 14-16]: R&D joint venture of three plastic producers. "If, in
-- addition to the parties to the joint venture (taken collectively), there are at least
-- four other independently controlled entities that possess comparable capabilities and
-- incentives ... the joint venture ordinarily would be unlikely to adversely affect
-- competition"; fewer than four: the Agency "would consider whether".
#ASSERT (`Example 3: the screen for a research and development joint venture` (LIST (`indep: good entity` "e1"), (`indep: good entity` "e2"), (`indep: good entity` "e3"), (`indep: good entity` "e4")) NOTHING) EQUALS (JUST `the joint venture ordinarily would be unlikely to adversely affect competition in the relevant research and development market`)
#ASSERT (`Example 3: the screen for a research and development joint venture` (LIST (`indep: good entity` "e1"), (`indep: good entity` "e2"), (`indep: good entity` "e3")) NOTHING) EQUALS (JUST `the agency would consider whether the joint venture would give the parties an incentive and ability collectively to reduce investment in, or otherwise to retard the pace or scope of, research and development`)
-- Example 3: a significant risk found: "the Agency would proceed to consider efficiency
-- justifications".
#ASSERT (`Example 3: the screen for a research and development joint venture` (LIST (`indep: good entity` "e1"), (`indep: good entity` "e2"), (`indep: good entity` "e3")) (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS (JUST `the agency would proceed to consider efficiency justifications for the venture`)
-- Example 3: an entity controlled by a party does not count.
#ASSERT (`Example 3: the screen for a research and development joint venture` (LIST (`indep: good entity` "e1"), (`indep: good entity` "e2"), (`indep: good entity` "e3"), (`indep: entity` "e4" "Party A" TRUE TRUE TRUE)) NOTHING) EQUALS (JUST `the agency would consider whether the joint venture would give the parties an incentive and ability collectively to reduce investment in, or otherwise to retard the pace or scope of, research and development`)

-- Example 4 [pdf page 17]: AgCo and FarmCo. Emission control technology: FarmCo is
-- neither an actual nor a potential competitor (it cannot develop around the patent),
-- and is a consumer of AgCo's technology: vertical. Farm equipment: horizontal.
#ASSERT (`3.3: the relationship of the parties in the market` (`indep: two parties` FALSE FALSE TRUE)) EQUALS `a vertical relationship`
#ASSERT (`3.3: the relationship of the parties in the market` (`indep: two parties` TRUE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS `a horizontal relationship`
-- Example 4: FarmCo's technology "does not significantly constrain" AgCo's: not actual
-- competitors in that technology market.
#ASSERT (`3.2.2: the parties are actual competitors in the technology market` (`indep: two technologies` FALSE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)

-- Example 5 [pdf page 18]: valve technology cross-licence. AgCo's own valve technology is
-- substitutable at comparable cost: actual competitors; and AgCo consumes FarmCo's:
-- vertical in part and horizontal in part. "Whether the firms license their valve
-- technologies to others is not important"; "Even if AgCo's use ... were solely captive".
#ASSERT (`3.3: the relationship of the parties in the market` (`indep: two parties` TRUE FALSE TRUE)) EQUALS `a relationship horizontal in part and vertical in part`
#ASSERT (`3.2.2: the parties are actual competitors in the technology market` (`indep: two technologies` TRUE FALSE TRUE)) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)
#ASSERT (`3.2.2: the parties are actual competitors in the technology market` (`indep: two technologies` TRUE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)

-- Example 6 [pdf pages 20-21]: Gamma's unused, non-improving process licensed with
-- exclusive territories to competing makers of X. No useful transfer of technology, so no
-- efficiency-enhancing integration: "likely to challenge the arrangement under the per
-- se rule as a horizontal territorial market allocation scheme".
#ASSERT (`3.4: the mode of analysis` (`indep: restraint` `market division among horizontal competitors` FALSE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS `the agencies will challenge the restraint under the per se rule`
-- Example 6: if the technology were an advance and used (integration): rule of reason.
#ASSERT (`3.4: the mode of analysis` (`indep: restraint` `market division among horizontal competitors` FALSE TRUE TRUE)) EQUALS `the agencies will apply a rule of reason analysis`
-- Example 6: the same whatever the form of IP: outside the safety zone (facially
-- anticompetitive), even with a small share, for patent, trade secret and copyright.
#ASSERT `indep: is outside` (`4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`indep: arrangement in full` `a patent` TRUE TRUE `indep: no transfer` (`indep: restraint` `market division among horizontal competitors` FALSE FALSE FALSE) FALSE (LIST (`indep: goods market` "X" 10 EMPTY))))
#ASSERT `indep: is outside` (`4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`indep: arrangement in full` `a trade secret` TRUE TRUE `indep: no transfer` (`indep: restraint` `market division among horizontal competitors` FALSE FALSE FALSE) FALSE (LIST (`indep: goods market` "X" 10 EMPTY))))
#ASSERT `indep: is outside` (`4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`indep: arrangement in full` `a copyright` TRUE TRUE `indep: no transfer` (`indep: restraint` `market division among horizontal competitors` FALSE FALSE FALSE) FALSE (LIST (`indep: goods market` "X" 10 EMPTY))))

-- Example 7 [pdf pages 24-25]: NewCo's exclusive licence to BigCo with exclusive dealing.
-- Vertical, so the exclusive licence "does not affect competition between the licensor
-- and the licensee"; the exclusive dealing is evaluated under the rule of reason; market
-- unconcentrated, small share of outlets, easy entry: none of those risk factors present;
-- "the evaluating Agency would be unlikely to challenge the arrangement".
#ASSERT (`4.1.2: what the agencies say of the license's exclusivity` (`indep: licence` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) (`indep: horizontals` FALSE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS (JUST `generally, the exclusive licensing raises no antitrust concern: there is no horizontal relationship among licensors, among licensees, or between the licensor and a licensee`)
#ASSERT (`5.4: exclusive dealing` (`indep: licence` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS (JUST `exclusive dealing arrangements are evaluated under the rule of reason`)
#ASSERT (`4.1.1: the considerations bearing on the risk of harm that are present` (`Market characteristics (4.1.1, 5.4)` WITH `the relevant markets are concentrated` IS FALSE, `entry into the relevant markets is difficult` IS FALSE, `supply and demand respond little to changes in price` IS FALSE, `the restraint affects a large proportion of the relevant markets` IS FALSE, `the restraint is of long duration` IS FALSE, `owners of competing technologies impose similar restraints on their licensees` IS FALSE, `competing licensees are subject to common restraints from a common licensor or competing licensors` IS FALSE)) EQUALS EMPTY
-- Example 7: on the Agency's conclusion that harm is unlikely (its finding): no challenge.
#ASSERT (`4.2: what the agencies do on their findings` (`indep: findings` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS (JUST `the agencies will not challenge the restraint`)

-- Example 8 [pdf pages 28-29]: two leading makers jointly assign non-blocking, substitutable
-- patents to a corporation that sets royalties. Horizontal in the technology market.
-- Absent efficiency-enhancing integration, joint marketing of competing patents is
-- horizontal price-fixing, challengeable per se.
#ASSERT (`3.2.2: the parties are actual competitors in the technology market` (`indep: two technologies` TRUE FALSE TRUE)) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)
#ASSERT (`3.4: the mode of analysis` (`indep: restraint` `naked price-fixing` FALSE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS `the agencies will challenge the restraint under the per se rule`
#ASSERT (`5.5: the mode of analysis of a collective restraint in a pool or cross-license` (`indep: restraint` `naked price-fixing` FALSE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS `the agencies will challenge the restraint under the per se rule`
-- Example 8: with integration, rule of reason, "However, the Agency may conclude that the
-- anticompetitive effects are sufficiently apparent, and the claimed integrative
-- efficiencies are sufficiently weak or not reasonably related to the restraints to
-- warrant challenge ... without an elaborate analysis".
#ASSERT (`3.4: the mode of analysis` (`indep: restraint` `naked price-fixing` TRUE TRUE FALSE)) EQUALS `the agencies will apply a rule of reason analysis`
#ASSERT (`3.4: what the agencies do with the restraint` (`indep: restraint` `naked price-fixing` TRUE TRUE FALSE) (`indep: findings` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS (JUST `the agencies will likely challenge the restraint without an elaborate analysis of particular industry circumstances`)

-- Example 9 [pdf page 34]: only blocking patents assigned: "the manufacturers are not in
-- a horizontal relationship with respect to those patents"; horizontal in goods. No
-- anticompetitive collateral restraints: "unlikely to challenge".
#ASSERT (`3.2.2: the parties are actual competitors in the technology market` (`indep: two technologies` FALSE TRUE TRUE)) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)
#ASSERT `3.3: the relationship has a horizontal component` (`indep: two parties` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT (`3.4: the mode of analysis` `indep: ordinary restraint`) EQUALS `the agencies will apply a rule of reason analysis`
#ASSERT (`3.4: what the agencies do with the restraint` `indep: ordinary restraint` (`indep: findings` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS (JUST `the agencies will treat the restraint as reasonable, without an elaborate analysis of market power or the justifications for it`)

-- Example 10 [pdf pages 36-37]: Omega's nominally non-exclusive licence to Delta,
-- "exclusive in fact" (the Discussion's finding); potential competitors, so horizontal in
-- the goods market; "The evaluating Agency would apply a merger analysis". Hence the
-- safety zone does not apply (n.86).
#ASSERT `3.3: the relationship has a horizontal component` (`indep: two parties` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT (`5.7: merger analysis of the transfer` (`indep: transfer` FALSE TRUE TRUE)) EQUALS `the agencies will apply a merger analysis: an exclusive license`
#ASSERT `indep: zone does not apply` (`4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`indep: arrangement in full` `a patent` TRUE TRUE (`indep: transfer` FALSE TRUE TRUE) `indep: ordinary restraint` FALSE (LIST (`indep: goods market` "drugs for the disease" 5 EMPTY))))
-- Example 10 read through n.85 alone (n.85 cites Example 10 as its instance of a licence
-- that "in substance transfers" the rights): the Example still says the Agency "would
-- apply a merger analysis", so this reader expects merger analysis, not "none".
#ASSERT NOT ((`5.7: merger analysis of the transfer` (`indep: transfer` FALSE FALSE TRUE)) EQUALS `section 5.7 calls for no merger analysis`)
